# Code owners.
#
# GitHub requests a review from the owner of every path a pull request touches.
# The point here is not gatekeeping — it is a single maintainer repo — but that
# the paths below are the ones where a change has consequences beyond the diff,
# so a review request on them is a useful signal rather than noise.

*                       @neramc

# Project memory. `.ai/` outranks docs/, prompts/ and the code itself in the
# SSOT order declared in CLAUDE.md, so a change here silently redefines what
# every future session believes about the project.
/.ai/                   @neramc
/CLAUDE.md              @neramc

# Append-only by rule. An edit to an existing ADR is a rewrite of history and
# should never appear in a diff; a new one at the end should.
/.ai/decisions.md       @neramc

# The design is frozen (ADR-0017/0018, owner-approved). Restyling an approved
# screen requires a new comp and re-approval before any code moves.
/design/                @neramc
/packages/ui/src/tokens.css   @neramc
/packages/ui/src/styles.css   @neramc

# Anything that changes what we fetch, how often, or from where. The crawler
# policy in .ai/security.md is binding and a source must be verified before its
# fetcher exists.
/.ai/data-sources.md    @neramc
/packages/ingest/       @neramc

# Deployment surface: schema migrations are forward-only, secrets and bindings
# live here, and CI is what stops the rest from shipping broken.
/apps/api/migrations/   @neramc
/apps/api/wrangler.toml @neramc
/.github/               @neramc
